# tools/g/geode_libraries_witness.rish -- the library index is generated, and still true.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. An index of what a tree contains is the fastest-rotting page a tree can own. Every
# module added makes it a little less true, and nobody notices, because an index is trusted rather
# than checked -- that is what an index is FOR. So this one is read off disk each run and compared,
# byte for byte, against the page on the shelf.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   The page on disk equals a fresh render. A module added without regenerating reds here.
#   The page says it is generated, so a reader knows not to spend effort editing it.
#   Every room it names has the README it claims, so no row points at a door that is not there.
#   The witness count is taken by REFERENCE, not by filename glob -- the glob reported zero for
#   `image` and `lotus`, 463 modules between them, because their proofs are named for what they
#   prove rather than where it lives. A confident wrong zero is worse than no number.
#   The module count asks git what the tree keeps, proven on real repositories in a temporary pen
#   by tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_control.sh. The `glow` room keeps a `.cache` of 108 generated
#   modules the repository ignores, and a plain `find` published 238 where the tree keeps 130 -- a
#   number that moved when somebody compiled and drifted with no commit behind it (REDS %216).
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. Whether each library is any good, or whether its README says anything true.
# This proves the index is honest about what exists, not that what exists is well made.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/geode_libraries_witness.rish

say "geode-libraries: Language EN -- an index is trusted rather than checked, which is exactly why it must be generated and compared."
say "geode-libraries: Style Radiant -- three claims. The page equals a fresh render. It says it is generated. And every room it names has the door it claims."
say "geode-libraries: Lens TAME -- the witness count is taken by reference rather than by filename, because a glob reported a confident zero for two rooms holding 463 modules; the module count asks git what the tree keeps, because a find counted 108 ignored build artifacts as modules of the `glow` room."

# The counting rule is proven before the page is trusted, and it is proven on real git repositories
# rather than described. A rule proven only where it passes cannot be told from a rule that counts
# every file on disk, which is precisely the rule this replaced.
let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "geode-libraries: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "geode-libraries: the control must reach its own verdict"
assert control.out contains "an ignored cache module stays out of the count -- read 1" else "geode-libraries: a module git ignores must stay out of the count"
assert control.out contains "the same three modules count when nothing ignores them -- read 3" else "geode-libraries: the rule must read the ignore list rather than the path"
assert control.out contains "an untracked, unignored module counts -- read 2" else "geode-libraries: a module written this minute is real and counts"
assert control.out contains "a room holding only ignored modules leaves the index -- read 0" else "geode-libraries: a room the tree keeps no module in leaves the index"
assert control.out contains "control_fail=0" else "geode-libraries: every planted reading must hold"

let fresh = run ["sh" "-c" "sh tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_scan.sh render | cksum"]
assert fresh.ok else "geode-libraries: a fresh render must succeed"
let onshelf = run ["sh" "-c" "cksum < docs-geode/libraries/README.md"]
assert onshelf.ok else "geode-libraries: the page must be readable"
assert (trim fresh.out) == (trim onshelf.out) else "geode-libraries: the page has drifted from the tree -- regenerate with rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/geode_libraries.rish write"
say "freshness GREEN -- the page equals a render taken this second"

let marked = run ["grep" "-cF" "This page is generated" "docs-geode/libraries/README.md"]
assert marked.ok else "geode-libraries: the page must tell a reader it is generated"
say "marker GREEN -- the page says plainly that it is generated"

# Every row must point at a README that exists. A row naming a door that is not there is the one
# failure an index can have that a reader cannot see from the index itself.
let doors = run ["sh" "-c" "miss=0; for p in $(grep -oE '\\]\\(\\.\\./\\.\\./[a-z-]+/README\\.md\\)' docs-geode/libraries/README.md | sed 's|](../../||; s|)$||'); do [ -f \"$p\" ] || miss=$((miss+1)); done; echo missing=$miss"]
assert doors.ok else "geode-libraries: the door check must run"
say doors.out
assert doors.out contains "missing=0" else "geode-libraries: every room named must have the README the row links to"
say "doors GREEN -- every row opens on a README that is there"

say "GREEN: geode-libraries -- the index equals a fresh reading of the tree, says it is generated, and every door it names is open."
